# Measured ceilings, floors and digests for the ratchets in
# .github/workflows/CI.yml, and for the one at the end of this file in
# .github/workflows/viewer.yml — the reader's workspace has a lane of its own
# because GitHub filters paths on a workflow's trigger rather than on one job
# of many, and a ceiling belonging to a second lane is still a ceiling and still
# belongs here. Sourced by the steps that enforce them, so the numbers live in
# exactly one place. .github/RATCHETS.md says what each one measures and prints
# the command that reproduces it, and
# bindings/python/tests/test_ratchet_documents_agree.py holds that page to this
# file.
#
# Every number here was measured, not chosen. Re-running the command beside a
# value on that page is how you check the value is still true.
#
# Which direction they move: ceilings down, in the commit that earns it. A step
# fails only when the count goes ABOVE its ceiling, so today's state always
# passes; when work removes violations, lower the ceiling in the same commit, or
# the ground it recovered is silently available to the next regression. Raising
# one is allowed and is meant to be conspicuous: it is a line in the diff with a
# reason beside it.
#
# The *_MIN_FILES floors point the other way, and are not a second ceiling by
# another name. They are the denominators: how much of the package a count had
# to be taken over. A count that fell because the run got narrower is not an
# improvement, and a step with no floor cannot tell the two apart -- it reports
# the fall and invites the next commit to ratchet down to it. Floors equal the
# measured count: they move up as the package grows, and down only in the
# commit that genuinely removes source files, with the reason beside them.
#
# The *_SUPPRESSION_SHA digests ratchet in no direction at all, because they
# are not counts. They record the settings a count was taken under -- the ones
# that decide whether a diagnostic is raised, which neither a ceiling nor a
# denominator can see. A count that fell because a rule was turned off is not
# an improvement, and it moves neither of the other two figures. These are
# replaced rather than raised or lowered, in the commit that changes the
# settings, alongside a re-measurement of the ceiling and the floor beside
# them. Same shape as .github/jscpd-baseline.json: what gets enforced is
# content identity, not a number.
#
# Every variable here must stay defined, and must stay in the shape its step
# compares: a whole number for the ceilings and the floors, sixty-four
# lower-case hexadecimal characters for the digests. The steps assert both
# before they compare anything, and fail when either is untrue: `[ 5 -gt "" ]`
# exits 2, which a shell `if` reads as false, so a variable deleted from this
# file would otherwise wave a genuine regression through while printing an
# empty ceiling. A figure of ten digits or more fails identically -- `[ 5 -gt
# 999999999999999999999999 ]` also exits 2 -- and is refused for the same
# reason. Deleting one is not how a ratchet is retired — remove its step.

# Ruff violations across the package under the declared configuration
# (select = ["ALL"], less the ignores it lists), file-level `# ruff: noqa`
# headers and inline noqa honoured: what ruff reports, not what it would report
# unsuppressed. Measured with ruff 0.16.3, the version the pyproject pins, by
# the change that last lowered it. A file-level header coming off a file exposes
# the violations it was hiding, so the commit that removes one raises this with
# that reason beside it; headers come off one file at a time.
# Lowered from 1157 to 1071 on 2026-10-04, by the fixes and the type work
# that went into 1.0.0 after its first candidate.
# Lowered from 1071 to 80 on 2026-10-08: every mechanical finding fixed, and
# every finding that needed a decision either fixed or kept with an inline
# noqa naming the fact that makes the rule not apply. What is left is the
# public-API shape (boolean positional arguments, which only a breaking change
# removes) and complexity (refactors), plus findings whose fix would change
# what a user sees.
RUFF_MAX=80

# Clippy and rustc warnings across the Rust workspace, all targets, counted as
# diagnostics that carry a lint code (the "N warnings emitted" summaries are not
# counted twice). 34 are in the core crate and 2 in the binding crate, and the
# binding's two are one site, a too_many_arguments on its internal registration
# function reported for the library and for its tests, left visible rather than
# suppressed. Toolchain-bound: the clippy job pins 1.94.0, the toolchain this
# was measured on, because a newer stable can add lints and a count that moves
# when nobody changed code is not a ratchet. Bumping the toolchain is a
# deliberate act, and the same commit re-measures this number. Not
# `-D warnings`: that would demand a mass fix in one go.
# Lowered from 39 to 36 on 2026-10-11 by the 1.0 hardening's second wave,
# measured on toolchain 1.94.0 that day.
CLIPPY_MAX=36

# Mypy errors under the strict configuration in bindings/python/pyproject.toml,
# across the package, its `exclude` list honoured. Counted off the summary line
# mypy prints whenever it completes, because `--output=json` carries no summary
# and an empty JSON file counts cleanly to zero -- which is under any ceiling,
# so a mypy that died would present itself as a mypy that found nothing. The
# step needs the third-party packages installed: with them absent the count
# rises rather than falls, because under `strict = true` every unneeded
# `# type: ignore` and every decorator that became `Any` is reported. Measured
# with mypy 2.1.0, the version uv.lock pins, by the change that last lowered it.
# Zero since 2026-10-04: the package type-checks clean in strict mode, so any
# error is a regression rather than ground still to win.
MYPY_MAX=0

# The denominator MYPY_MAX is only comparable over: the number of source files
# mypy has to have checked before its error count says anything about the
# package. 222 is every module under gaspatchio/ outside the `exclude` list,
# with a stub checked instead of the module it shadows. Necessary and not
# sufficient -- MYPY_SUPPRESSION_SHA below is the rest of it. Deleting a module
# with no stub beside it is -1 here and -1 on PYRIGHT_MIN_FILES; deleting one
# together with the stub that shadows it is -1 here and -2 there.
# Raised from 219 on 2026-09-30 by three modules the audit record's read-back
# added: frame/graph/_model_files.py and frame/graph/verify.py (an audit
# file's evidence checked against the files in hand) and engines/_versions.py
# (the versions a run states). None has a stub, so pyright's floor moves by
# the same three.
# Raised from 222 on 2026-10-04 by four modules with no stub:
# _git_operand.py and _lfs.py (gspio diff's git: operand and the Git LFS
# pointer check), _warning.py (GaspatchioWarning) and frame/plan_writes.py
# (a write into the query plan, read). Pyright's floor moves by the same four.
# Raised from 226 to 227 on 2026-10-08 by _version.py (the installed version,
# shared by gaspatchio.__version__ and gspio --version). The four package stubs
# deleted the same day (scenarios, mortality, assumptions, util) leave this
# figure alone: mypy now checks each __init__.py in place of its stub.
# Raised from 227 to 231 on 2026-10-10: _table_lifecycle.py (the scenario
# run's own stacked tables, which had left this floor one behind), then
# three modules the 1.0 hardening added with no stub: _beside.py (a model
# imports the files beside it), frame/_row_operations.py (a row operation over a
# per-period column refused on a timeline frame) and
# frame/lowering/_polars/rendering.py (an exact quotient rendered as its
# operator). column/proxy_aware_expr.pyi arrived in the same batch and leaves
# this figure alone: mypy checks the stub in place of the module.
# Raised from 231 to 232 on 2026-10-11 by assumptions/_processing.py, with no
# stub: the steps that turn a source into a table's processed frame, moved out
# of assumptions/_api.py so gspio verify --assumptions can re-read a file as a
# table without importing the authoring surface.
# Raised from 232 to 234 on 2026-10-11 by two modules with no stub:
# scenarios/_targets.py (a scenario shock names the one table or column it
# moves, or the plan refuses) and engines/_agreement.py (section 11.1.12's
# agreement rule, written once as one Polars pass per line, which gspio compare
# reads and diff --results will).
# Raised from 234 to 235 on 2026-10-11 by errors/policy_locator.py, with no
# stub: a kernel's refusal names the policy that failed, read off the frame,
# where the kernel itself cannot know the row.
# Raised from 235 to 236 on 2026-10-13 by frame/lowering/value_reads.py, with
# no stub: the registry that refuses a table, mortality, curve or schedule read
# inside an engine fragment, so the fingerprint moves with its table.
# Raised from 236 to 239 on 2026-10-20 by three modules with no stub, all the
# scenario plan binding its own targets: _scenario_reads.py (a read of a
# shocked table lowered against that table stacked for the batch),
# scenarios/_binding.py (which reads a run binds, and a model reading the axis)
# and scenarios/_columns.py (column shocks rewriting a model-point column).
# Raised from 239 to 240 on 2026-10-20 by frame/graph/xlsx_export.py, with no
# stub: a one-policy workbook laid out from the audit record, every cell the
# record's double (GSP-201).
# Raised from 240 to 243 on 2026-10-20 by three modules with no stub, all the
# lineage questions answered from an audit file (GSP-197): frame/graph/lineage.py
# (the one walk af.graph and the file reader share), graph.py (read_artifact and
# GraphDocument) and graph_cli.py (gspio graph).
# Raised from 243 to 244 on 2026-10-20 by frame/lowering/kinds.py, with no
# stub: the kind of value a fill, a branch, a shift's fill_value, a substitution
# or a bound is, and the refusal when it is not the column's.
# Raised from 244 to 246 on 2026-10-20 by frame/graph/diff_results.py and
# frame/graph/values_moved.py, with no stub: what moved between two versions'
# results files, and the shape of the report's values member (GSP-196).
# Raised from 246 to 247 on 2026-10-20 by _output_target.py, with no stub: why
# a path a gspio command was told to write has no place to go.
# Raised from 247 to 248 on 2026-10-21 by _shown.py, with no stub: a name read out
# of a file shown to a reader as text, never as code or a terminal command.
# Raised from 248 to 252 on 2026-10-22 by frame/_across_rows.py (a read across
# rows where the frame is not the book), frame/graph/selection.py and
# frame/graph/selection_replay.py (the selection record and its replay) and
# frame/lowering/lift.py (a raw Polars predicate read into the frame's tree),
# each with no stub.
# Raised from 252 to 253 on 2026-10-22 by frame/_row_choosing.py, with no stub:
# why af.head(), af.unique() and the other row pickers are not model steps, and
# what to write instead.
# Raised from 253 to 254 on 2026-10-29 by frame/lowering/_polars/comparisons.py,
# with no stub: a per-period comparison read exactly, never through a double.
MYPY_MIN_FILES=254

# SHA-256 of the configuration mypy resolved (mypy.main.process_options, so a
# mypy.ini dropped in beside pyproject.toml is seen), every key of its options
# snapshot less a named few: scope (exclude, exclude_gitignore), the host
# (python_executable, and platform reduced to whether it was overridden) and
# the command line. From bindings/python,
#   .venv/bin/python ../../.github/type_suppression_fingerprint.py mypy
# prints it, and --document prints what was hashed. Replaced, with MYPY_MAX and
# MYPY_MIN_FILES re-measured under the new settings, in the commit that
# changes them.
MYPY_SUPPRESSION_SHA=67afd8f9332c3914fc71a888f64dafa7a5405fe27001cdbd0e040e0513dd8544

# Pyright errors (not warnings; the run reports one) under [tool.pyright] in
# bindings/python/pyproject.toml, read out of --outputjson, which a pyright that
# did not run cannot write. Configured before it was measured, so the count does
# not depend on whether .venv/bin is on PATH, and typeCheckingMode is written
# down rather than inherited. Measured with pyright 1.1.411, the version
# uv.lock pins, by the change that last lowered it.
# Zero since 2026-10-04, as MYPY_MAX is.
PYRIGHT_MAX=0

# The number of files pyright has to have analysed, read out of the same JSON
# document as PYRIGHT_MAX. 245 is every .py and .pyi under gaspatchio/ outside
# the `exclude` list: pyright analyses both members of a module/stub pair,
# where mypy checks only the stub.
# Raised from 242 on 2026-09-30 by the same three modules as MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 245 on 2026-10-04 by the same four modules as MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Lowered from 249 to 246 on 2026-10-08: four package stubs deleted (−4;
# scenarios, mortality, assumptions and util __init__.pyi, which hid their
# source docstrings from the API reference) and _version.py added (+1).
# Raised from 246 to 251 on 2026-10-10 by the same four modules as
# MYPY_MIN_FILES, plus column/proxy_aware_expr.pyi, which pyright analyses
# beside its module.
# Raised from 251 to 252 on 2026-10-11 by assumptions/_processing.py, the same
# module as MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 252 to 254 on 2026-10-11 by the same two modules as
# MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 254 to 255 on 2026-10-11 by errors/policy_locator.py, the same
# module as MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 255 to 256 on 2026-10-13 by frame/lowering/value_reads.py, the
# same module as MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 256 to 259 on 2026-10-20 by the same three modules as
# MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 259 to 260 on 2026-10-20 by frame/graph/xlsx_export.py, the same
# module as MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 260 to 263 on 2026-10-20 by the same three modules as
# MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 263 to 264 on 2026-10-20 by frame/lowering/kinds.py, the same
# module as MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 264 to 266 on 2026-10-20 by the same two modules as
# MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 266 to 267 on 2026-10-20 by _output_target.py, the same module as
# MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 267 to 268 on 2026-10-21 by _shown.py, the same module as
# MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 268 to 272 on 2026-10-22 by the same four modules as
# MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 272 to 273 on 2026-10-22 by frame/_row_choosing.py, the same
# module as MYPY_MIN_FILES.
# Raised from 273 to 274 on 2026-10-29 by frame/lowering/_polars/comparisons.py,
# the same module as MYPY_MIN_FILES.
PYRIGHT_MIN_FILES=274

# SHA-256 of [tool.pyright] as parsed out of bindings/python/pyproject.toml,
# less include and exclude, and of whether a pyrightconfig.json exists in
# bindings/python (pyright reads that instead of pyproject.toml). Pyright has no
# way to report its effective configuration, so the file is what is hashed.
# `ignore` is inside the digest: it suppresses diagnostics while leaving
# filesAnalyzed untouched, so no other value here can see it. From
# bindings/python,
#   .venv/bin/python ../../.github/type_suppression_fingerprint.py pyright
# prints it. Replaced, with PYRIGHT_MAX and PYRIGHT_MIN_FILES re-measured, in
# the commit that changes the settings.
PYRIGHT_SUPPRESSION_SHA=a94c7167b52aa4fa16ef6cb1513b18235dd6a67834a46892d971d0750429a63b

# The reader's bundle: viewer/dist/viewer.js and viewer/dist/viewer.css
# together, at gzip level 9, as `node build.mjs` prints it from viewer/. The
# artifact inlined beside them in an exported page is the model's size and is
# not counted. Written at exactly the size Node 24.21.0 builds when it last
# moved -- 572,280 JavaScript bytes and 35,826 CSS bytes before compression,
# 2026-09-30, measured on macOS x64 with that Node, which gives the Viewer job's
# own figure for the tree before it byte for byte -- so no capability lands
# without this line moving: raise it in the commit whose
# capability earned the bytes, saying here what they bought, and lower it when
# bytes come out. Dependency-bound: viewer/package-lock.json pins what makes up
# most of the bytes, so a figure that moves with nothing under viewer/src
# touched is a dependency moving, and that commit re-measures this number.
# The figure is also Node's: zlib's output moves between Node releases and
# platforms (a Mac on Node 24.3.0 compresses the same bytes to 189,046), so
# the lane pins its Node exactly and CI's figure is the gate. Bump
# node-version in viewer.yml and CI.yml and re-measure this line together.
#
# Raised by 90 bytes from 188059 on 2026-09-29 -- 99 for viewer/src/views/rows.ts,
# less 9 the three commits before it had freed. rows.ts draws the grid's rows in whole blocks of sixteen so that a scrub changes the
# table's rows once a block rather than on every frame -- one of the changes
# that took both scrubs back inside the frame budget on a 2-core CI runner.
# Raised 4 more, to 188153, in the commit after it: one CSS rule that paints
# each of the grid's body rows on its own, so a period step repaints the two
# rows the cursor moved between rather than every row in the window.
# Raised 141 more, to 188294, when the grid learned the height of its sticky
# header and of any scrollbar that takes room from it: a row the cursor reaches
# moving down had landed under the bottom edge of what a reader can see, the
# row they had just moved to, and now lands inside it.
# Raised 56 more, to 188350, on 2026-09-30 for one sentence: the comparison
# page's advice on two books it cannot compare now names ModelIdentity.of and
# the export config that takes it, the way a Python export names its files,
# where it had named a constructor no export is written with any more.
# Raised 438 more, to 188788, in the commit after it, for the comparison page
# reading the results file each run recorded, as gspio diff does: a results
# file that differs is listed under a heading of its own with a sentence saying
# the file moved and gspio compare says whether the numbers did, and a results
# file only one run named is said not to have been compared. Before it,
# neither the page nor the command read the results files.
# Raised 444 more, to 189232, in the commit after it, for the page naming a
# cause only where the record does: a column whose values moved under
# unmoved definitions reads "the book moved" only where the two books differ
# or an assumption or injection entry moved, and where the record rules the
# ordinary causes out it says nothing in the record explains the move and
# names the check that finds the line. Before it, a column rewritten in the
# query plan was said to be the book moving under the same book.
# Raised 577 more, to 189809, in the commit after it. "The book moved" is
# said on the book alone, since a re-sourced basis moves the fingerprints that
# read it and so explains no line marked data; books that could not be
# compared, a policy neither document names and a change of producer are each
# said as what they are, the last as a candidate rather than a cause; a line
# that moved by no more than section 11.1.12 allows agrees within the
# specification's tolerance, by the rule gspio compare applies; and the results
# sentences name the checksum, the platform and whether the two results agree.
# Raised 1394 more, to 191203, on 2026-10-04, for three things a reader sees.
# The Audit View's strip states the tier census -- how many calculations sit at
# each tier, zeros included, naming the ones below core, each taking the reader
# to its node -- and the Model tab states it under the holes line, so "every
# column is accounted for" is not read as "every line is in the format's own
# vocabulary" (1080). The grid's row labels stick down the left as one column
# rather than a compositing layer each, and stay level with their rows at any
# zoom (188). A comparison page names each side by the label the command gave
# it, a long one giving way from its start (126).
# Raised 432 more, to 191635, on 2026-10-10, for the comparison page saying
# which advice applies when the results files differ, as gspio diff now does:
# where the two runs' graph fingerprints differ it says gspio compare will
# refuse them and points at the calculations listed and the two files side by
# side; where only the book moved it says compare measures each column over the
# same policies and refuses books of different sizes. Before it the page always
# advised running gspio compare, which refuses every before/after change of a
# model. Measured on Node 24.21.0 on 2026-10-10: 191203 before, 191635 after.
# Raised 1898 more, to 193533, on 2026-10-11, for the reader showing every
# member the audit record carries: the Model tab states the model's own files
# (model.modules), the library versions that produced the numbers
# (producer.versions) and why a git revision is not recorded; the Table panel
# states the file a table was read from and how it was shaped; a selected cell
# shows, and copying it copies, every digit the file holds. Measured on Node
# 24.21.0 on 2026-10-11: 191635 before, 193533 after.
# Raised 344 more, to 193877, on 2026-10-11, for the comparison page naming a
# library that moved under one release, in gspio diff's own words ("library:
# polars X -> Y; extension sha differs"), where before it said the producer
# changed and printed the same release on both sides. Measured on Node
# 24.21.0 on 2026-10-11: 193533 before, 193877 after.
# Raised 139 more, to 194016, on 2026-10-11, for the Model tab showing the
# formulas fingerprint beside the graph fingerprint, each with one line saying
# what it covers. Measured on Node 24.21.0 on 2026-10-11: 193877 before,
# 194016 after.
# Raised 511 more, to 194527, on 2026-10-20, for the reader drawing a read's
# period window the way it draws an offset: the cone's loop labelled with the
# window, the grid outlining every cell of it, and the proof line saying
# "reads first...t". Measured on Node 24.21.0: 194016 before (2026-10-11),
# 194527 after (2026-10-20).
# Raised 1471 more, to 195998, on 2026-10-20, for the comparison page showing how
# far each change moved over the whole book: per entry "moved in k of n
# policies, worst x% at P, t", identity-only lines greyed and labelled, a
# within-band chip, the re-export commands for the selected entry, and the
# cross-check of the page's own policy against the CLI's book-wide block
# (GSP-196). Measured on Node 24.21.0 on 2026-10-20: 194527 before, 195998 after.
# Lowered 105, to 195893, on 2026-10-20: the comparison page stopped refusing two
# artifacts whose model.source_path differs (it refuses what gspio diff refuses,
# as decided 2026-09-19), which removed that refusal's text. Measured on Node
# 24.21.0 on 2026-10-20.
# Raised 1327, to 197220, on 2026-10-30, for the comparison page naming a moved
# hole, the lines under it, and the model's own files. Measured
# by the Viewer job on Node 24.21.0 on 2026-10-30 (595,084 JavaScript and 38,064
# CSS bytes), and again on Linux with that Node from the tree that set it; it
# had first been estimated at 197208 from Node 24.3.0.
# Raised 515, to 197735, on 2026-10-30, for a cheaper period step on the comparison
# page's scrub, which missed its frame budget on slow runners: the strip, React
# Flow's tree and the Node tab behind memos, the grid's follow worked out without
# reading the layout, a cone box's value line drawn on its own, and the grid's scroller
# painting the page's white so it scrolls as a layer.
# Measured on Linux with Node 24.21.0 from the tree that set it (596,395 JavaScript
# and 38,088 CSS bytes).
VIEWER_BUNDLE_GZIP_MAX=197735
